        "section": "music-theory",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Tonal Harmony - Advanced",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nCOMMON-PRACTICE PERIOD (≈ 1600–1900):\n  A unified harmonic language shared across Baroque, Classical, Romantic\n  Characterized by:\n    ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n    │ 1. FUNCTIONAL TONALITY: T → PD → D → T drives structure │\n    │ 2. DIATONIC CORE: most chords from the key's scale      │\n    │ 3. CONTROLLED CHROMATICISM: non-diatonic notes prepared │\n    │ 4. VOICE LEADING RULES: smooth motion, resolved tensions│\n    │ 5. HIERARCHICAL FORM: keys organized around a tonic key │\n    └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-TONAL-HARMONY.md#003",
      "path": [
        "06-TONAL-HARMONY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
