        "root_concepts": "[tonal, harmony]",
        "section": "music-theory",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Tonal Harmony - Advanced",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "EXAMPLE: C major → G major\n  In C major: Am  (= vi in C)\n  In G major: same chord Am = ii in G\n  → Am is the pivot chord (vi = ii)\n  After the pivot, V7 of G (D7) → G confirms the modulation"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-TONAL-HARMONY.md#011",
      "path": [
        "06-TONAL-HARMONY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
