      "text": "EXAMPLE: C major → E major (third relation)\n  C major chord: C–E–G\n  E major chord: E–G♯–B\n  Common tone: E (appears in both chords)\n  The E in C major becomes the root of E major\n  G→G♯ moves by chromatic half step"
    },
