        "section": "music-theory",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Tonal Harmony - Advanced",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "AUGMENTED 6TH as pivot (German):\n  The German augmented 6th chord in one key is enharmonically identical\n  to a dominant 7th in another key (a tritone away):\n  In C major: A♭–C–E♭–F♯ (Ger+6) = G♯–B♯–D♯–F♯ (if respelled = A♭7 dominant)\n  This allows modulation to the tritone-related key via an enharmonic pivot\n  Used famously in Schubert's \"Winterreise\" and Wagner\n```"
    },
