        "current_path": "music-theory/06-TONAL-HARMONY.md",
        "id": "maxim:music-theory:tonal-harmony",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "music-theory",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[tonal, harmony]",
        "section": "music-theory",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Tonal Harmony - Advanced",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Most often appears in FIRST INVERSION: N⁶ (= ♭II⁶)\n  F in the bass (the 3rd of D♭ major): D♭/F → G7 → C"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-TONAL-HARMONY.md#033",
      "path": [
        "06-TONAL-HARMONY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:music-theory:06-tonal-harmony, git-history:music-theory:06-tonal-harmony]",
