        "root_concepts": "[tonal, harmony]",
        "section": "music-theory",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Tonal Harmony - Advanced",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "HARMONIC FUNCTION: Pre-Dominant (like iv or ii°)\n  N⁶ → V → I  (or N⁶ → i⁶₄ → V → i in minor)\n  The D♭ \"steps down\" by a half step to C (tonic), or\n  the F steps down by a semitone to E (3rd of I)"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-TONAL-HARMONY.md#034",
      "path": [
        "06-TONAL-HARMONY.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
